  "dataHandlingTitle": "How your data is handled",
  "dataHandlingPhoneTitle": "Stored on this phone",
  "dataHandlingPhoneBody": "Factory profile, confirmed bills, production, solar plans and the last calculated reports. Bill photos only if you turn on \"Keep bill images\". Delete everything any time in Settings.",
  "dataHandlingServerTitle": "Sent to our server",
  "dataHandlingServerBody": "The cropped bill photo (to read it), and the numbers needed for each calculation: monthly quantities, amounts, production, roof outline. The server keeps nothing: no database, no stored images, no logged request contents.",
  "dataHandlingGoogleTitle": "Sent to Google",
  "dataHandlingGoogleBody": "The cropped bill photo is passed to Google's Gemini API to read the values, under Google's Gemini API terms. On Google's free (unpaid) tier, Google may use the content to improve its products and human reviewers may read it; on a paid (billing-enabled) project it does not use it for that. Crop out personal details before uploading. The app never asks Gemini for names, addresses, consumer or meter numbers.",
  "dataHandlingNasaTitle": "Sent to NASA POWER",
  "dataHandlingNasaBody": "For solar estimates our server asks NASA POWER for sunlight data at the roof's approximate location (rounded). No other data is sent.",
  "limitationsTitle": "Known limitations",
  "limitationsBody": "• Scope 1 and 2 from bills and fuel receipts: grid electricity, natural gas, diesel, LPG and furnace oil. No Scope 3, refrigerant leaks, coal or biomass.\n• The emissions report is a draft until its method and format are checked against your buyer's requirements.\n• Bill-reading accuracy has only been measured on a few sample bills. Always check values.\n• Names are hidden automatically only when printed in English letters. Cover handwritten or Bangla names by hand.\n• The unusual-use check flags statistical outliers against production; it cannot identify causes and does not prove waste.\n• Measured savings compare the whole factory before and after an action; weather, product mix or other changes can also play a part.\n• Solar results are estimates only.\n• Emission factors come from published government sources (shown with source and year in the report). Update them when newer editions appear and confirm they match the buyer's rules.\n• The app token is weak protection, adequate for a demo only.",
  "demoNeedsEmpty": "Demo data can only be loaded when the app has no real bills or production. Export or delete your data first.",
  "carbonStale": "Your data changed after this report was calculated. Update it.",
