  "actionSuggestionsHint": "Start with the ones marked “Best for you”. Tap a card to see the steps.",
  "actFixAirLeaksSteps": "With machines stopped (lunch or a holiday), walk the floor and listen for hissing at hoses, couplings and air guns.\nTie a tag on each leak and write it on a list.\nRepair or replace the parts, then check again every month.",
  "actSwitchOffIdleSteps": "Choose one person on each floor to be in charge of switching off.\nSwitch off machines, lights and fans at lunch, after the last shift and on holidays.\nPut a simple checklist on the wall and sign it every day.",
  "actLowerAirPressureSteps": "Ask the machine suppliers what air pressure each machine really needs.\nLower the compressor setting a little at a time while production keeps running.\nStop at the lowest setting where every machine still works well.",
  "actSteamLeaksSteps": "Walk the steam lines and mark leaks and steam traps that blow steam all the time.\nRepair them and insulate bare hot pipes and valves.\nSend hot condensate water back to the boiler.",
  "actGeneratorHoursSteps": "Keep a log book of when the generator starts and stops.\nSwitch back to grid power as soon as it returns.\nEach week, compare the log with the power-cut times.",
  "actLedLightingSteps": "Find the lights that are on the longest (production floor, 2–3 shifts).\nReplace those tube lights and bulbs with LED first.\nChange the rest when the old ones fail.",
  "actServoMotorsSteps": "Count the sewing machines that still have clutch motors (they hum even when nobody sews).\nAsk a supplier for a price to fit servo motors.\nStart with one line, compare its electricity, then do the rest.",
  "actPowerFactorSteps": "Look on the electricity bill for a power-factor (PF) penalty or a low PF value.\nAsk a licensed electrician to check the capacitor bank.\nRepair or add capacitors until the penalty is gone from the bill.",
  "actRooftopSolarSteps": "Open the Solar page and tap your roof for a free estimate.\nGet quotes from 2–3 solar companies.\nAsk an engineer to check that the roof can carry the panels.",
